  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Capacity Building for the development of the Myanmar potato sector</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to develop a knowledge base and expertise pool for the potato sector in Myanmar, along with providing hands-on training to farmers. More specifically, the goal of this capacity-building project is to develop a structure and the initial content of a locally relevant and easily accessible knowledge base and train 25 potato value chain professionals (PVCPs) who will be able to contribute to strategy development and will act as trainers and advisors for farmers and students. The project should aim to train a minimum of 1,000 farmers on the basics of Good Agricultural Practices (GAP) for successful and profitable potato growing by the end of the project.</narrative>
  </description>
